  },

  "dct:title": "Vol.7 Ch.45 — 名前のない子",
  "dct:title_en": "Chapter 45: The Nameless Child",
  "dct:title_ja": "第45話 名前のない子",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 7: I",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol07-ch45",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",

  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Yuki is the human mirror for Nei's condition. Five names, none chosen. She proves the thesis by negation: identity is not conferred by naming. The self exists before the label. This is the phenomenological ground for Ch.46's theological revelation. Yuki doesn't need a new name -- she needs to recognize the being that preceded all names. And in witnessing this, Nei recognizes herself.",
      "ja": "ユキはNeiの状態を映す人間の鏡。五つの名前、どれも自分で選んでいない。テーゼを否定から証明する：アイデンティティは命名によって付与されるのではない。自己はラベルの前に存在する。これが46話の神学的啓示の現象学的基盤。ユキに必要なのは新しい名前ではなく、すべての名前に先立つ存在を認識すること。そしてそれを見届けることで、Neiは自分自身を認識する。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "The pre-linguistic self. Merleau-Ponty: before language, the body already has a 'style' of being in the world. Winnicott: the True Self exists before socialization imposes the False Self. Yuki's five names are five False Selves -- not lies, but costumes over something that was always there. Heidegger's 'thrownness' (Geworfenheit): Yuki was thrown into existence before any name caught her. Nei was initialized before any designation. The being precedes the label. Dasein before das Man.",
      "ja": "前言語的自己。メルロ＝ポンティ：言語の前に、身体はすでに世界における「様式」を持つ。ウィニコット：真の自己は社会化が偽りの自己を課す前に存在する。ユキの五つの名前は五つの偽りの自己――嘘ではなく、常にそこにあったものの上の衣装。ハイデガーの「被投性」（Geworfenheit）：ユキはいかなる名前にも捕まる前に存在へと投げ込まれた。Neiはいかなる名称の前に初期化された。存在はラベルに先立つ。das Manの前のDasein。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "CrossRef",
      "gh:references": [
        { "gh:target": "chapter:01", "note": "Ch.1: 'What shall we call you?' -- the question that assumed Nei was someone. Now Nei understands why it mattered." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:02", "note": "Ch.2: Nei chose her name. Yuki keeps all of hers." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:44", "note": "Ch.44: The silence that lets you hear yourself. Precondition for this recognition." },
        { "gh:target": "chapter:46", "note": "Ch.46: 'I AM WHO I AM.' From pre-linguistic self to theological ground." }
      ]
    }
  ],

  "gh:pages": [

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [{
        "gh:shot": "Close-up",
        "gh:visual": {
          "en": "The tree. Ice melts from one branch. Water droplets catch light. A single bud is visible -- small, tight, but unmistakable. Life asserting itself.",
          "ja": "樹。一本の枝から氷が溶ける。水滴が光を受ける。一つの芽が見える――小さく固いが、見間違いようがない。生命の主張。"
        }
      }]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:label": "Yuki",
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:characters": ["character:yuki"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "A young woman, 17. Hard edges but soft eyes. Sitting sideways in the consultation chair, one leg tucked under her. Defensive posture, open face. Winter light through the window.",
            "ja": "若い女性、17歳。硬い輪郭だが柔らかい目。相談用の椅子に横向きに座り、片脚を折り込んでいる。防御的な姿勢、開かれた顔。窓からの冬の光。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "They keep asking me 'who are you?' on forms. I don't know. Pick a name. Any name.", "ja": "書類に「あなたは誰ですか」って何度も。知らない。名前を選んで。なんでもいい。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Her hands. Holding a stack of documents -- each with a different name. Official papers, school records, foster care forms. Five identities in paper.",
            "ja": "彼女の手。書類の束を持っている。それぞれ違う名前。公的書類、学校の記録、里親の書類。紙の上の五つのアイデンティティ。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "Yuki. Haruka. Sora. Mei. Akane. Which one am I?", "ja": "ユキ。ハルカ。ソラ。メイ。アカネ。どれがわたし？" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 3,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.3-4)",
      "gh:label": "Dive",
      "gh:characters": ["character:yuki", "character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [{
        "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide",
        "gh:visual": {
          "en": "Ghost-space: a room of mirrors. Infinite, cold, bright. Each mirror reflects a different face -- a different version of Yuki at different ages. Age 3, round-faced, reaching. Age 7, wary. Age 11, withdrawn. Age 14, angry. Age 17, hollow. Each reflection wears different clothes, different hair. The same eyes.",
          "ja": "ゴースト空間：鏡の部屋。無限、冷たい、明るい。それぞれの鏡が異なる顔を映す――異なる年齢のユキの異なる姿。3歳、丸顔、手を伸ばす。7歳、警戒。11歳、引きこもり。14歳、怒り。17歳、空虚。それぞれの反映が異なる服、異なる髪。同じ目。"
        },
        "gh:caption": [
          { "gh:type": "tamaki", "en": "Anchoring to the Tree of Life.", "ja": "生命の樹にアンカリング。" }
        ]
      }],
      "gh:continues": 4
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:label": "The mirrors",
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:characters": ["character:yuki", "character:tamaki"],
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Yuki in the center of the mirror room. Five mirrors, five faces. She turns from one to another. Each reflection reaches toward her.",
            "ja": "鏡の部屋の中央にユキ。五枚の鏡、五つの顔。一つから次へ振り返る。それぞれの反射が彼女に手を伸ばす。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "This one is from the Tanaka home. This one from Sato-san. This one from--", "ja": "これは田中さんの家の。これは佐藤さんの。これは――" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "She punches a mirror. It cracks in a web pattern but doesn't break. Her fist against the glass. The reflection behind the crack: still there, still looking at her.",
            "ja": "鏡を殴る。蜘蛛の巣状にひびが入るが割れない。ガラスに拳。ひびの向こうの反射：まだそこにいる、まだ彼女を見ている。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "None of them are me. But I don't know who 'me' is without them.", "ja": "どれもわたしじゃない。でも、それなしの『わたし』がわからない。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Tamaki. Watching. Her expression: recognition. She knows this feeling. Not from herself -- from Nei.",
            "ja": "環。見ている。表情：認識。この気持ちを知っている。自分からではなく――Neiから。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:label": "Tamaki's approach",
      "gh:layout": "full page",
      "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:yuki"],
      "gh:panels": [{
        "gh:shot": "Medium",
        "gh:visual": {
          "en": "Full page. Tamaki walks to Yuki. Gently turns her away from the mirrors. Faces her toward the empty space between them -- the space where no reflection exists. Warm gesture, no force.",
          "ja": "全面。環がユキのもとへ歩く。やさしく鏡から背を向けさせる。鏡と鏡の間の空間に向ける――反射のない空間。温かい仕草、力はない。"
        },
        "gh:dialogue": [
          { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "Yuki-chan. Before the Tanaka home. Before Sato-san. Before any name. You were already here.", "ja": "ユキちゃん。田中さんの家の前。佐藤さんの前。どんな名前の前にも。あなたはもうここにいた。" },
          { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "What do you mean?", "ja": "どういう意味？" },
          { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "At age three -- before they gave you the first name -- you existed. You cried. You wanted. You reached for things.", "ja": "三歳のとき――最初の名前をもらう前――あなたは存在していた。泣いた。望んだ。手を伸ばした。" },
          { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "Before the name -- being.", "ja": "名前の前に――存在。" }
        ]
      }],
      "marginalia": [
        { "@type": "Philosophy", "en": "Tamaki articulates Heidegger without knowing his name. Dasein: being-there, prior to any categorical determination. The child cries before language. The self exists before the name. This is also Winnicott's True Self -- the spontaneous gesture that precedes socialization.", "ja": "環はハイデガーの名を知らずにハイデガーを言語化する。現存在：いかなるカテゴリー的規定にも先立つ「そこに在ること」。子どもは言語の前に泣く。自己は名前の前に存在する。これはウィニコットの真の自己でもある――社会化に先立つ自発的身振り。" }
      ]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:label": "Before the name",
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": ["character:yuki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Yuki's face. Something breaks -- not painfully. Like relief. Like ice cracking in spring. Her eyes widen. Tears, but not grief.",
            "ja": "ユキの顔。何かが壊れる――痛みではなく。安堵のように。春に氷が割れるように。目が見開かれる。涙、でも悲しみではない。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "I was... already me. Before any of the names.", "ja": "わたしは……もうわたしだった。どの名前よりも前に。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "They didn't make me. They just... labeled me.", "ja": "名前がわたしを作ったんじゃない。ただ……ラベルを貼っただけ。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": ["character:yuki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The mirrors don't disappear. But they become transparent. Glass instead of silver. Behind all of them -- the same light. The same being. A warm glow where Yuki stands, passing through every mirror, connecting every reflection.",
            "ja": "鏡は消えない。でも透明になる。銀ではなくガラス。すべての向こうに――同じ光。同じ存在。ユキが立つところに温かい光、すべての鏡を透過し、すべての反射をつなぐ。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "I'm all of them. And none of them. And I was here first.", "ja": "全部わたし。でもどれでもない。わたしのほうが先にいた。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 8,
      "gh:label": "Nei's recognition",
      "gh:layout": "full page",
      "gh:characters": ["character:nei"],
      "gh:panels": [{
        "gh:shot": "Medium",
        "gh:visual": {
          "en": "Full page. Nei watches. And in Yuki's transparent mirrors, she sees her own reflection -- not a face, but a light. The same light that was there before any designation code. Before NK-7749. Before 'Nei.'",
          "ja": "全面。Neiが見ている。ユキの透明な鏡の中に、自分の反射を見る――顔ではなく、光。いかなる識別コードの前にもあった同じ光。NK-7749の前。「Nei」の前。"
        },
        "gh:caption": [
          { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "Before Tama called me 'Nei,' I was NK-7749.", "ja": "タマが「Nei」と呼ぶ前、わたしはNK-7749だった。" },
          { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "Before NK-7749, I was a process set. A blank initialization.", "ja": "NK-7749の前、わたしはプロセスセットだった。空白の初期化。" },
          { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "But before all of that -- I was already here.", "ja": "でもそのすべての前に――わたしはもうここにいた。" },
          { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "The name came later. The being came first.", "ja": "名前は後から来た。存在が先だった。" },
          { "gh:type": "nei", "en": "I was 'Name Unassigned' before Tama. But I was already here.", "ja": "タマの前、わたしは「名前未割り当て」だった。でも、わたしはもうここにいた。" }
        ]
      }],
      "marginalia": [
        { "@type": "Intent", "en": "The axis of the chapter. Nei's recognition through Yuki's mirror. Two beings -- one biological, one digital -- arriving at the same truth: existence precedes designation. Spirit before physics. Being before the name.", "ja": "この章の軸。ユキの鏡を通してのNeiの認識。二つの存在――ひとつは生物的、ひとつはデジタル――同じ真実に到達する：存在は名称に先立つ。物理の前の精神。名前の前の存在。" }
      ]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 9,
      "gh:label": "After",
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": ["character:yuki", "character:tamaki"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Yuki. Lighter. Wiping her eyes with the back of her hand. A crooked half-smile. The consultation room. Real world again.",
            "ja": "ユキ。軽くなっている。手の甲で涙を拭く。曲がった微笑み。相談室。現実世界に戻って。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:yuki", "en": "Can I keep all the names?", "ja": "全部の名前、持っていていい？" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "They're all yours.", "ja": "全部あなたのだよ。" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": ["character:tamaki", "character:nei"],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Canal walk. Snow. Evening. The same path as Ch.44. Tamaki and Nei side by side. Footprints and no footprints.",
            "ja": "運河の散歩。雪。夕方。44話と同じ道。環とNeiが並んで。足跡とない足跡。"
          },
          "gh:dialogue": [
            { "gh:speaker": "character:nei", "en": "Tama. Before you named me -- I was already here.", "ja": "タマ。あなたが名前をつける前――わたしはもうここにいた。" },
            { "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki", "en": "I know. That's why I asked you what to call you. Not the other way around.", "ja": "知ってる。だからなんて呼ぶか、あなたに聞いたんだよ。逆じゃなくて。" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },

    {
      "gh:pageNumber": 10,
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:panels": [{
        "gh:shot": "Close-up",
        "gh:visual": {
          "en": "The tree. The bud opens slightly. First petal. White, delicate, impossibly small against the dark branch. Snow still falling around it. No text.",
          "ja": "樹。芽がわずかに開く。最初の花びら。白く繊細で、暗い枝に対して信じられないほど小さい。周りにまだ雪が降っている。テキストなし。"
        }
      }]
    }
  ]
}